---
title: Texture loading
description: Load URL textures with reactive state, cancellation, caching, and cleanup.
---

`useTexture(...)` is the adapter lifecycle wrapper around the framework-neutral URL loader. Svelte and Vue defer loading until client mount; all adapters dispose their current bitmaps on unmount.

## Input and result

```ts
const loaded = useTexture(
	() => ['/textures/albedo.png', '/textures/normal.png'],
	{ colorSpace: 'srgb', generateMipmaps: true }
);
```

The URL input is a `string[]` or lazy `() => string[]`. Svelte and Vue also accept a lazy options provider; React accepts an options object.

| Result | Type |
| --- | --- |
| `textures` | `CurrentReadable<LoadedTexture[] &#124; null>` |
| `loading` | `CurrentReadable<boolean>` |
| `error` | `CurrentReadable<Error &#124; null>` |
| `errorReport` | `CurrentReadable<SpektralErrorReport &#124; null>` |
| `reload()` | `Promise<void>` |

Read `.current` in frame callbacks and subscribe when UI must react.

## Options

| Field | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `colorSpace` | `'srgb'` | Loaded texture metadata and decode default |
| `requestInit` | — | Forwarded fetch options; its `signal` also cancels this caller |
| `decode` | Derived | `createImageBitmap` conversion, premultiplication, and orientation |
| `signal` | — | External cancellation |
| `update`, `flipY`, `premultipliedAlpha`, `generateMipmaps` | — | Metadata copied to each loaded texture |

Linear color defaults decode `colorSpaceConversion` to `'none'`; sRGB defaults to `'default'`. `premultiplyAlpha` defaults to `'default'` and `imageOrientation` to `'none'`.

Each `LoadedTexture` contains its URL, `ImageBitmap`, dimensions, color-space and optional upload metadata, plus an idempotent `dispose()`.

## Concurrency and cleanup

- `reload()` aborts the active request and queues a fresh load.
- Request versions prevent stale results from replacing newer results.
- A failed batch aborts sibling requests and disposes textures that already completed.
- Successful replacement disposes the previous bitmap list.
- `AbortError` is treated as cancellation and does not populate error state.
- Other failures, including lazy URL/options provider errors, populate both the raw error and normalized report and always clear loading state.

`signal` and `requestInit.signal` both cancel the calling load. A shared fetch remains active while
another caller still references it.

Only `GET` and `HEAD` requests without a body can share a reference-counted blob request. They must
have the same URL, normalized fetch options, color space, and decode options. Requests using other
methods or any body always run independently. A cache entry is removed when its final consumer
releases it; an unsettled request is aborted at that point.

Pass each loaded bitmap through `state.setTexture(...)`. See [Textures](/docs/textures) for upload and sampler behavior.
